# Codex assets: revalidate on every load instead of caching for an hour, so a
# production merge lands on the NEXT page load with no hard-refresh and no
# per-deploy step.
#
# "no-cache" does not mean "never cache". It means "cache, but always check with
# the server before reusing": the server returns a tiny 304 Not Modified when a
# file is unchanged (~free), or the new file ONCE when it actually changed. So the
# real re-download happens exactly once per deploy, automatically.
#
# Why this and not a ?v query on the scripts: a version query on an entry module
# does NOT refresh its ES `import`ed sub-files; revalidation covers every file,
# and keeps CSS + JS in lockstep (no "new CSS / old JS" window).
#
# To trade the per-load 304 pings for an up-to-60s staleness window after a
# deploy, swap "no-cache" for "max-age=60".
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(html|js|mjs|css)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
